  "steps": [
    "Preheat the oven to 220°C. Line a baking tray with baking paper if needed.",
    "Rinse the quinoa, then add it to a pan with the water. Bring to a boil, reduce to a low simmer, cover, and cook for about 15 minutes until the water is absorbed and the quinoa is fluffy. Turn off the heat and let it stand for 5 minutes, then fluff with a fork.",
    "On a large tray, toss the sweet potato, broccoli, red pepper, red onion, and chickpeas with olive oil, salt, black pepper, and paprika. Spread them out in a single layer.",
    "Roast for 20 to 25 minutes, turning once halfway through, until the vegetables are tender and browned at the edges.",
    "In a small bowl, whisk together the tahini, lemon juice, water, maple syrup, garlic, and salt until smooth and pourable. Add a splash more water if needed.",
    "Divide the spinach between two bowls. Top with quinoa, roasted vegetables, and chickpeas. Drizzle over the tahini sauce and finish with pumpkin seeds.",
    "Serve immediately while the vegetables are warm and the sauce is creamy."
